  The admission estimate 10× compact + 256 MB: for the big window: compact 20.8 GB total... if the widest window holds ~23.7% of precursors and similar share of peaks → ~5 GB compact → need = 50 GB + 0.25. Hmm, if budget = 0.75×(MemAvailable+RSS)... The measured 12 GB/window average is suspiciously close to need-average (10×0.87=8.7+0.26≈9 GB). Actual usage 12 GB > estimate 9 GB → the estimate UNDER-estimates the big windows? If the big window actually needs 3×10=30+ GB but uses ~35 GB (FragGrid!), the 10× multiplier under-covers exactly at the peak-driving structure (FragGrid ~7× compact for trace-dense windows). The estimate is defensible for the trace phase (wmap+sub ≈ 3× + traces) but NOT for the score phase (FragGrid alone can reach ~7× compact). Evidence: peak occurs in loop. Also inflight accounting: `need` held constant through whole window; actual footprint varies 3× over phases.

  What's the peak driver: 8 concurrent windows × (trace-phase transient wmap+sub OR score-phase FragGrid). If big windows run concurrently, FragGrids dominate. Also note: FragGrid flat holds intensities for ALL fragment traces, while the fragment traces' xic vectors are freed at :2432 — good.

