  Peak-driving allocation: candidates: (a) FragGrid.flat for the widest window (~35 GB), (b) MTD trace vectors + EPD copies for big window, (c) sub[] band copies. The instrumented answer: log RSS per stage per window — the code already logs rss at phase ends but not per-window-stage. The [mem] logs at :2402 (window done) print RSS per window completion — could extract from logs. Peak driver most likely the widest window's trace→grid overlap: sub copies (7-9 GB) + MTD traces + Trace XICs + FragGrid construction: buildFragGrid copies xic into flat while xic still live: 4.3e9×8 + XIC 4.3e9×16 = 34.7 + 69 = 104 GB for the widest window?! That can't be — peak total is 151.7 with 55 base and other windows. Hmm, so 8.5M×510 must not be the widest window on THIS file, or support is smaller. The comment hedges "up to" / "within 2x of wrap". If actual support avg ~50: flat = 8.5e6×50×8 = 3.4 GB, XIC = 6.8 GB. Fine. I should be careful: cite the comment as evidence the design anticipates up to ~510, and note the discrepancy is measurable. The 12 GB/window decomposes roughly: wmap 2× + sub 2× + traces/XIC ~4-6× + grid ~4× compact — sum of phase peaks ~10-14× compact ≈ matches 12 GB vs 0.87 compact ≈ 14×. So 10×+256MB admission UNDER-estimates by ~1.4× on average and more on big windows → admission control is over-optimistic: it admits 8 windows believing 8×8.9=71 GB while they actually consume 97 GB. On this node it survived; on a smaller node it OOMs. Defensible? Direction is right (proportional to compact), multiplier measured on S23 (~5.8 GB vs 0.56 compact ≈ 10.4×) but S23 windows may be smaller/lower-threshold; the multiplier is threshold-dependent (ms2_noise 10 → more traces → FragGrid bigger). Make the multiplier adaptive: measure actual RSS delta per completed window and re-fit. Or set 14×. Low-risk fix.

  Also memory mitigation: don't materialise wmap at all — partition compact frames into bands directly and materialise 12 band PeakMaps (saves wmap ≈ 2× compact transient AND the sub copy: total trace-phase footprint from 4× to 2× compact). Also frees earlier. Output-neutral if band edges computed identically (sample every 97th peak from compact mzq — same values, order? sample loop at :956-957 iterates map spectra in order, peaks i+=97; compact frames preserve order → same sample → same edges. Deterministic.)

